ecc-curve-kdf: report the recommended KDF of the NIST curves in TPM2_ECC_Parameters

Classification: profile setting.

The kdf of TPMS_ALGORITHM_DETAIL_ECC is an informative recommendation that
may be TPM_ALG_NULL (Part 2; deprecated in version 185, where the reference
reports TPM_ALG_NULL for every curve). tpm-rs, like the references before
version 185, reports KDF1_SP800_56A with SHA-256 (P-192/P-224/P-256),
SHA-384 (P-384) or SHA-512 (P-521), and TPM_ALG_NULL for the other curves.
diff --git a/TPMCmd/tpm/cryptolibs/implementations/EccRef/CryptEccMain.c b/TPMCmd/tpm/cryptolibs/implementations/EccRef/CryptEccMain.c
--- a/TPMCmd/tpm/cryptolibs/implementations/EccRef/CryptEccMain.c
+++ b/TPMCmd/tpm/cryptolibs/implementations/EccRef/CryptEccMain.c
@@ -313,6 +313,29 @@
         parameters->keySize = curve->keySizeBits;
         // This field is deprecated and it never actually correlated to behavior from the Reference Code.
         parameters->kdf.scheme = TPM_ALG_NULL;
+        // tpm-rs differential testing: the recommended KDF is informative and
+        // may be TPM_ALG_NULL (Part 2, TPMS_ALGORITHM_DETAIL_ECC); tpm-rs (like
+        // the references before version 185) reports KDF1_SP800_56A with the
+        // hash of the curve's security strength for the NIST curves.
+        switch(curveId)
+        {
+            case TPM_ECC_NIST_P192:
+            case TPM_ECC_NIST_P224:
+            case TPM_ECC_NIST_P256:
+                parameters->kdf.scheme = TPM_ALG_KDF1_SP800_56A;
+                parameters->kdf.details.kdf1_sp800_56a.hashAlg = TPM_ALG_SHA256;
+                break;
+            case TPM_ECC_NIST_P384:
+                parameters->kdf.scheme = TPM_ALG_KDF1_SP800_56A;
+                parameters->kdf.details.kdf1_sp800_56a.hashAlg = TPM_ALG_SHA384;
+                break;
+            case TPM_ECC_NIST_P521:
+                parameters->kdf.scheme = TPM_ALG_KDF1_SP800_56A;
+                parameters->kdf.details.kdf1_sp800_56a.hashAlg = TPM_ALG_SHA512;
+                break;
+            default:
+                break;
+        }
         parameters->sign       = curve->sign;
         //        BnTo2B(data->prime, &parameters->p.b, 0);
         found = found
